# Verify after changes

After finishing a batch of code edits (not after every single keystroke/tool call), run quality gates before considering the task done.

## Commands

```bash
npm run lint
npm test
```

- Prefer `CI=true` when installing or rebuilding natives so Vitest keeps the Node ABI.
- If only docs/rules/markdown changed, skip tests; still run lint if JS/TS/config was touched.
- If changes are isolated to one area, you may run a focused test first (`npm test -- tests/unit/…`), then full `npm test` before finishing.
- Fix failures you introduced before handing off; do not leave red lint/tests.

## Do not

- Skip verification because the change “looks small” if it touches runtime or test code.
- Commit as part of verification unless the user asked to commit.
